              ToolMessage(content='All searches completed successfully. I checked flights around a few ideal windows for a Paris destination wedding and found great options. Here\'s my analysis and shortlist.\n\n## ✈️ London → Paris — Flight Shortlist\n\n### 💰 Cheapest options\n| Route | Times & Duration | Cabin | Price | Book |\n|-------|------------------|-------|-------|------|\n| LTN → CDG (Luton → CDG) | 05 Oct 2026 19:40 → 22:00 (1h 20m) | Economy | **45 EUR** | [Book](https://kiwi.com/u/g2cx6t) |\n| LTN → CDG (Luton → CDG) | 01 Oct 2026 19:30 → 21:50 (1h 20m) | Economy | 49 EUR | [Book](https://kiwi.com/u/6fj8g6) |\n\n### ⏱️ Shortest options (1h 10m direct)\n| Route | Times & Duration | Cabin | Price | Book |\n|-------|------------------|-------|-------|------|\n| SEN → CDG (Southend → CDG) | 13 May 2027 10:10 → 12:20 (1h 10m) | Economy | **55 EUR** | [Book](https://kiwi.com/u/7jzxug) |\n| SEN → CDG (Southend → CDG) | 05 Oct 2026 11:10 → 13:20 (1h 10m) | Economy | 52 EUR | [Book](https://kiwi.com/u/sdvczz) |\n| STN → CDG (Stansted → CDG) | 05 Oct 2026 15:35 → 17:45 (1h 10m) | Economy | 60 EUR | [Book](https://kiwi.com/u/5frsdv) |\n\n### 🌸 Best wedding-season options (May/June 2027)\n| Route | Times & Duration | Cabin | Price | Book |\n|-------|------------------|-------|-------|------|\n| SEN → CDG (Southend → CDG) | 13 May 2027 10:10 → 12:20 (1h 10m) | Economy | 55 EUR | [Book](https://kiwi.com/u/7jzxug) |\n| SEN → CDG (Southend → CDG) | 24 May 2027 11:10 → 13:20 (1h 10m) | Economy | 59 EUR | [Book](https://kiwi.com/u/gmqg76w) |\n| SEN → CDG (Southend → CDG) | 07 Jun 2027 11:10 → 13:20 (1h 10m) | Economy | 58 EUR | [Book](https://kiwi.com/u/yk32cj) |\n| LGW → CDG (Gatwick → CDG) | 16 May 2027 08:10 → 10:30 (1h 20m) | Economy | 61 EUR | [Book](https://kiwi.com/u/b8w9v7) |\n\n---\n\n### 📝 My recommendation\n\n**If you want the best wedding weather** — I\'d book the **SEN → CDG easyJet flight on 13 May 2027 (55 EUR)**: it\'s the shortest option (just 1h 10m), lands at CDG by lunchtime (perfect to settle in before the festivities), and is the cheapest spring option. Late May/early June is the sweet spot for a Paris wedding — rose gardens in full bloom, long golden evenings, and mild temperatures.\n\n**If you want the absolute lowest price** — the **LTN → CDG 05 Oct 2026 flight at just 45 EUR** is a steal, and Paris in early autumn is still beautiful with gorgeous fall light (though a touch cooler and shorter days).\n\nAll flights above are non-stop, 1h 10m–1h 20m, Economy class. Note: these easyJet fares include a personal item only — you\'ll want to add a cabin/checked bag for wedding attire if needed.\n\nFun fact: Paris has been a romantic wedding destination for centuries — couples can actually get married on the Eiffel Tower itself, and a "vin d\'honneur" (wedding toast) in a Parisian garden is the stuff of dreams! 💍✨\n\nBon voyage et félicitations! 🥂', name='search_flights', id='fe75b44a-020d-4fa7-b5b2-92c261305a2c', tool_call_id='call_89ee049d44584cbaac3d38fe'),
              ToolMessage(content="I've completed my searches (12 web searches). Based on my research, here's a summary of the best wedding venue options in Paris for 100 guests, ranked considering price (lowest), capacity (closest to 100), and reviews (highest).\n\n## Top Recommendations for a 100-Guest Paris Wedding\n\n### 🥇 Best Value + Perfect Capacity: Le Camondo\n- **Capacity:** Exactly 100 guests\n- **Price:** €1,000 – €8,400 venue hire; in-house packages €100–€300 pp\n- **Details:** Elegant 19th-century mansion in Paris (8th arr.), exclusive use, beautiful garden and veranda options, external catering permitted. *Caveat: limited/no reviews yet on Bridebook.*\n\n### 🥈 Best Reviews + Low Venue Cost: Hôtel Alfred Sommier\n- **Capacity:** Up to 180 guests (comfortably fits 100)\n- **Price:** From €3,500 (venue hire, excluding catering)\n- **Reviews:** 4.5★ (542 reviews)\n- **Details:** Prestigious historic hôtel particulier in the 8th arr., Louis XV/XVI salons, private garden, 97 rooms on-site for guests, external caterers welcome — one of the best value-to-quality ratios in central Paris.\n\n### 🥉 Best All-Inclusive Value: Hôtel Particulier Montmartre\n- **Capacity:** Up to 200 guests (fits 100)\n- **Price:** From €11,500 (all-inclusive peak season)\n- **Reviews:** 4.3★ (2,776 reviews)\n- **Details:** Exclusive boutique hotel with Paris's largest private hotel garden in Montmartre; Michelin-praised restaurant; in-house catering and full exclusivity included.\n\n### 🇫🇷 Convenient City Option: Musée de Montmartre\n- **Capacity:** 30–350 guests depending on space (banquet up to 250, cocktail 350)\n- **Price:** €4,200 – €13,800\n- **Details:** Historic venue with Renoir gardens and Sacré-Cœur views; dry hire allows any caterer. *Caveat: limited reviews listed.*\n\n### 💎 High-End Budget Option: Musée Rodin\n- **Capacity:** ~100 (up to 120 seated in Hôtel Biron)\n- **Price:** €12,000 – €16,000 indoor rental; larger garden events from ~€18,000–22,000\n- **Details:** Iconic gardens and sculpture setting in the 7th arr.; spectacular but among the priciest — total event costs run high.\n\n### 🚢 Unique Mid-Priced Option: Croisières en Seine (boat)\n- **Capacity:** ~100 guests\n- **Price:** €94 pp (festive evening cruise, 5h) for 100+ guests\n- **Details:** Seine river cruise with Eiffel Tower views; dinner + service included.\n\n---\n\n**My top pick balancing all three criteria:** **Le Camondo** (exact 100-guest capacity with the lowest venue hire from €1,000) though it lacks reviews. If you want proven quality with excellent reviews, **Hôtel Alfred Sommier** (4.5★, from €3,500) is the strongest overall recommendation — affordable, highly rated, and centrally located for a 100-guest wedding in Paris.", name='search_venues', id='cf8fd83a-e689-407b-b450-ac218e050022', tool_call_id='call_0dfe87fafc8841eba9fb33f4'),
